{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The numerically exact six-stage fusion is slower than the vendor pointwise kernels, so I’m not committing it as the final design. The promising route is one Triton pass whose FP32 add/multiply instructions explicitly prohibit contraction; that can preserve every eager rounding boundary without six launches. I’m prototyping that locally before changing the submitted entry point."}}
